WEBVTT

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:16.830
I can't do it now, but I won't give up

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.980
Because I've already woken up

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.050
The burning excitement reflects the times

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.770
My burning soul

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.500
No

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:02.660
We'll be right back.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.320
Escape from side one.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:48.780
The mobile suit's in your team.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.400
We expect more, especially from Titan pilots.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.540
But, sir...

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.280
It seems Lila's team is performing better than our troops.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.040
That's not exactly true, sir.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.420
Are you defending Jared?

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.980
No, sir, but the enemy...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.820
...exhibits an unusual power. You should take it into consideration.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.160
What are you getting at?

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.360
I've only heard stories about the White Base.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.780
But if the legends are true, that ship would have given me an impression similar to the Argama.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.900
What gives you that feeling?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.080
Well, at first it looks defenseless, but it becomes more dangerous as you get closer.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.020
This paradox is especially true for the Gundam Mark II.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:26.310
It even looks amateurish, but then shows its true power and retaliates ferociously.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.960
...Jamaicom, the...

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.940
Every ship appears to be heading for the old side 4 region.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.630
What? They must be desperate to enter the debris cluster just to lose us.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.310
They might be... new types.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:43.800
Don't be ridiculous. New types? There's no such thing.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.510
They're just the results of bogus media hype.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.660
You're making me a regular AU pilot?

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.280
Naturally, after seeing what you did out there.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.980
But I took off with the Gundam on my own, so I thought you'd throw me in the brig...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:09.820
punishment that's what I suggested relax Camille we're joking the Mont Blanc's pilots are now

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:14.700
aboard the Argama so our complement is full however I'd like to see how much further we

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:20.900
could develop your special abilities so now I'm a guinea pig for new types there are other research

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.990
institutes for that kind of thing that's not my business I'm more interested in your role as

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.830
part of the ship's crew the Argama is a military ship

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.110
But I'm not a soldier! I'm too young!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.530
During the one-year war, there were many soldiers your age who fought with the white-faced crew.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.560
And overall, throughout the Earth-Sphere, there's almost no such thing as an old soldier.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.070
I know, but I'd like to think it over first.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.860
I'm of the same opinion as Commodore Blex. Very interested in your abilities.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.880
Just because you're interested, it doesn't make it right to send young people out to war.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:03:59.960
Don't get-

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:05.940
Do you know why the Earth Federation's chosen to conceal the whereabouts of Amuro Ray?

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.120
He was the new type famous for piloting the very first Gundam. He was a hero.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:14.000
That's right. It only goes to show the Earth Federation doesn't know what it's doing.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:19.550
The souls of the planet's residents are pulled down by gravity so they can't fly like they should.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.580
So how is my becoming a pilot going to change any of that?

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.260
Well, for one thing, the spirits of the...

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:27.600
That has nothing to do with me!

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:28.820
Doesn't it?

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:29.980
Well, will I...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.560
Did I get all the benefits of being an officer on the Argama?

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.100
That's a possibility.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.490
Why did you become a soldier, Lieutenant?

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.350
Why do you want to know?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.340
I'd like to know your reasons.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.260
I guess it's because it's the only way I can make a living.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.900
That's probably why I never got married.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.560
The ship is now entering the Side 4 region.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:04:59.980
Residential...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.360
Modules ready for lockdown.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.040
All crew members change into normal suits.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.380
Be on special alert.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:26.580
You're in, Lieutenant.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.600
What do you want?

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.030
You shouldn't need me for anything right now.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.380
Why'd you stand up for me in front of Jemai Khan?

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.720
Oh, sorry.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.210
You were saying something about Jemai Khan?

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:48.520
I told you how I wanted to lead the Titans one day, didn't I?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.870
To do that, I have to deal with guys like him on my own terms.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.060
I didn't ask you to try and protect me like that.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.280
I just wanted you to show me how to fight in space.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.560
I don't think you were really listening to what I was saying.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.040
Huh?

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.120
I was trying to explain to him about the Argama.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.780
Protecting you was the last thing on my mind.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.270
Okay, so what's all this new type stuff about?

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.460
What are you looking at me for?

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:19.670
Commander Jemai Khan, it appears that Grips is in the process of beginning its move.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:23.500
Finally. And the enemy?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.040
Their ship is moving through the debris cluster.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.820
That means either side too.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.800
Or the moon.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.350
We've got a drifting object detected to starboard.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:40.910
Got it. Swinging bow.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:49.420
There's a small rock directly to port.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.660
Lieutenant Emma has excellent eyesight.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.020
That's the third one.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.970
Well, she isn't a Titan oppos...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.710
for nothing. X-Titan.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.680
Don't forget that. At this point, there's

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:07.700
no way of determining whether the Argama

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.860
is going to side one, side two,

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.640
or the moon. That's why

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.480
I propose we divide our fleet into...

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:18.040
Lieutenant, I am the one running this briefing.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.560
Sir, we just wanted to

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.040
return the favor to the Alexandria

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.740
for the repairs she did on our mobile suits.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.640
Since we're not Titans, I propose

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.750
we return to the Bosnia. We'll

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.970
pursue and close in on the...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.460
Argama from a different direction.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.380
You seem well motivated, but don't go

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.400
jumping into battle just because you find the

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.850
enemy. I've heard that you're the type who

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.310
enjoys war, Lieutenant. Those are

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.640
biased opinions, sir. Whatever.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.820
You will be in charge of what to

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.760
do when you contact the enemy, but your

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.820
main objective will be to meet up with

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.440
us. Sir, let's go.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.090
Yes, ma'am. Lieutenant Lila, would you like

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.980
to talk about it? No. I...

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.550
I already knew what Chimai Khan would say.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:02.850
Then why'd you push his buttons?

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:07.410
I wanted to show you why I dislike those kinds of men, Jared.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:14.160
Lila, what do you say we get together for a drink next time we meet?

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.780
I think we can do that.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:16.940
Thanks, that'd be great.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:20.800
Be a real soldier and then I can open my heart and tell you many things.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.670
That's something to look forward to.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.700
You've got what it takes to become a real soldier, with a little bit of work.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.310
Observers, take up your positions.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:48.690
Observers, to your positions.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:49.790
Lieutenant Quatro.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:50.580
Yes, sir.

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.940
Where is Lieutenant Emma?

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:53.640
Why, sir?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.500
Uh, well, I need to talk to her.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.520
Understood, sir. I'll have her come up to the bridge to see you later.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.070
Not yet? You still haven't found anything?

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.470
Don't be so impatient.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.650
Well, it looks like they're nowhere near side one.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:18.760
I found them.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.390
Are you sure it's them?

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.330
The radar's indicating a ship with the same shape as the Argama.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.090
I'm positive it's them.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.540
Then we guessed right.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:28.640
So, what do you think your chances are?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:29.880
I'm not too sure.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.170
this point but we'll attack anyway the titans aren't the only force around here but captain

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:45.640
you're making too much of me well you see it's actually colony 30 in sight captain there's

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:50.540
something i want you to see it should make it clear why we started our movement against the

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.900
earth federation government sir

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:36.630
The Argama has just docked at Colony 30, sir.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:39.310
Colony 30? But that's where...

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.520
That's where those space noids were wiped out during that riot.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.830
Why would the Aeyug want to visit there?

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.770
They might be trying to hide something.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:51.960
You know, because of its present condition, it might be perfect for a secret base.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.160
I'm gonna check it out.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:55.570
Go around and let us in by a civilian gate.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.130
That way they won't be able to see us enter the colony.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:10:59.910
Shouldn't you wait for the...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.180
Xandria to get here first before you do that?

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.640
Don't you think we should have a report fully prepared

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.520
for Commander Jem'aikon when he does arrive?

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.020
You've got a point.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.910
I'm only going to see what they're doing.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:15.720
Return when you find out if it's their base or not.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:16.520
Understand?

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:41.050
What are those?

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:44.120
They were once people. Mummies.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:45.240
Mummies?

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.110
They dried out because the colony mirrors weren't working.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:16.640
How can bodies just be left like this?

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.700
There are too many of them to bury.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.490
How could someone massacre all these people?

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.710
Because they're not actually taking lives with their own hands.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.960
If they don't see the bodies, it's hard for them to feel the pain involved in the process.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.280
I guess so.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:49.820
Are they the tanks of poison gas?

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.560
Looks like there's power here.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.070
The Aeug might be using this colony.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.590
Only a body.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:28.130
This colony is dead.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:29.970
But that's-

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.680
Just another reason why this would be a perfect location for the Ayukes base.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.510
Good point. We'll go check the spaceport.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:41.840
I'll use this.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.000
They didn't know what was happening until it was too late.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.160
Lieutenant Emma, you probably feel that the Anti-Earth Union Group

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.240
was somehow responsible for the political rally that took place here.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.470
However, the people on Earth weren't concerned with anything

00:13:58.470 --> 00:13:59.950
but the redevelopment of their own planet.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.330
and didn't give a thought to the welfare of space-noids.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.480
So what's wrong with them having a demonstration or two?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:14.010
And they were merely proposing that we human beings should leave the planet Earth alone,

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.230
letting it recover through its own natural processes,

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:21.400
and that all of mankind would be better off living in outer space instead.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:24.380
So they were peaceful, but Basque responded with this?

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:25.520
What do you think?

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:26.370
I don't know.

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.350
Right.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:33.670
You're just a kid.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:35.880
Why are you wearing that pilot suit?

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:37.960
I really don't know.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.640
It's kind of a long story.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.240
Are you a member of the AU?

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:43.180
Camille, where are you?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.430
Don't make a sound, kid.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.860
You're working for the Titans, aren't you?

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:51.420
No, I'm not.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.460
Too far, you'll get lost.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:57.430
That's a machine.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.070
Have you met Emma before?

00:15:59.290 --> 00:15:59.850
Well, yeah.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.250
Weren't you one of the pilots that...

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:03.550
But I still don't understand.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.450
Why overreact like this?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.630
Fear motivated their actions.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.480
People living in space were getting used to their environment.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.860
The Earth Federation was afraid of how these space-noids were adapting.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.920
They might become new types.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:16.670
Yes.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.720
They think of new types as superhumans with extra powers.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:24.160
And they're afraid that one day they'll even become the ruling class on Earth.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.420
Can people commit mass murder for that reason alone?

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:29.150
Of course they can.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:29.970
Some people take...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.260
lives for a small amount of money. Bask's decision makes much more sense than that.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:43.250
Yarling! Who are you? Lieutenant Lyla. It's all a lie. Bask would never think of killing so many

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:48.480
people for a reason like that. Have you taken a look around you? You just believe in the propaganda

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:53.890
spread by the remnants of the Zabi family who ruined Zeon. Did you ever stop to think that maybe

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:58.960
the Earth Federation is becoming the next Zabi family? What do you mean? They want to keep the

00:16:58.960 --> 00:16:59.600
earth to themselves.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:08.170
Too late.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.570
She must have entered this colony with her mobile suit.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:15.210
Let's get back to the Argama.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:15.630
Right.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.630
My hunch wasn't that bad.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.480
She's a good fighter.

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.960
And he only has one Salamis-class ship.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:29.740
That's only three mobile suits.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:34.310
Why don't you have Camille lead the attack, and your Rick Diaz team will support him?

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.370
Is this some kind of test for Camille?

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:38.650
I'm just checking the performance of the Mark II.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.820
Argama, Rick Diaz team will cover your flanks.

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:50.720
Roger that.

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:53.180
I'll be using Lieutenant Apoli's mobile suit.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.450
Gundam Mark II, moving out.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:07.010
Let's do it.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:07.900
You're cleared.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:29.970
Sir, his pilot...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:58.900
the Gundam. This is the kid who was wearing

00:18:58.900 --> 00:18:59.600
the pilot suit.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:04.190
Didn't you hear what Lieutenant Quattro said about the Earth Federation?

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.630
You can't win with a big moat, kid.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:10.980
You fight, I have to shoot back.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.060
He's really good.

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:19.360
That Mark II, was he always the pilot?

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:25.530
Protecting light flashes from a battle next to Colony 30, sir.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.170
It seems as if Lieutenant Lila was correct.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.820
He must be a new type.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:33.930
But he's just a kid.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.970
He's not even a real pilot.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:50.260
There's no way to lose to a child.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:56.010
Lieutenant, yourself. You're panicking.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:19:59.980
Disappear.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:05.000
Commander Jumai Khan, send some reinforcements!

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:07.450
Wait till the enemy uses up its resources.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:12.020
Also, this will teach you an important lesson if you want to be a better officer, Lieutenant.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:16.690
A soldier must be able to control his personal emotions at all times.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:11.160
Just as I said to Jamicon, don't take him lightly, Jared. He's not a normal child at all.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:21.120
I just said that this kid wasn't normal. This kind of judgment automatically results in hostility within my mind.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:26.160
I guess it's typical of us old types. We just can't help it.

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:34.900
What a shame.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:39.890
Stop it, Lieutenant.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:40.990
The battle's over.

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:47.510
You could be a real soldier.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.930
What were you trying to tell me, Lila?

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:56.940
Congratulations.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:59.960
Let me be the first to shake your hand as a full-fledged...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:08.520
You really are like a second Armour All-Ray.

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:11.550
I agree. You're the real thing, Camille.

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:16.190
Stop it! I'm not too sure I want to commit to the life of a soldier just yet.

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:21.120
It's my life. I'll make the decisions about it by myself.

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:26.300
Something unusual is happening within his mind.

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:56.650
On his own, wanting to avenge the death of Lila, he and his Galbaldi soon find themselves in a desperate battle against the Gundam Mark II within the moon's gravitational field.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:23:59.880
In the meantime, the AU...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.120
preparing for a large-scale operation to break the deadlock.

00:24:04.348 --> 00:24:04.848
NEXT

00:24:05.024 --> 00:24:06.464
On Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam.

00:24:07.356 --> 00:24:08.776
The Dark Side of the Moon.

00:24:09.148 --> 00:24:11.188
You will see the tears of time.
